# Apple signing + notarization credentials.
#
# Copy to `.signing-env` (gitignored), fill in the values for your
# own developer account, then run `npm run tauri:build:signed`
# from native-fork/ — the wrapper script (scripts/build-signed.sh)
# loads this file, exports the env vars, and runs the bundler.
#
# Each value lives in a different place in your developer account:
#
#   APPLE_TEAM_ID
#     ─ developer.apple.com → Account → Membership Details → Team ID
#       Looks like J4UJD4Z33J. Same team for direct-dist + App Store.
#
#   APPLE_ID
#     ─ The email you sign in to developer.apple.com with.
#
#   APPLE_PASSWORD
#     ─ App-specific password from appleid.apple.com → Sign-In and
#       Security → App-Specific Passwords. NOT your Apple ID password.
#       Format: abcd-efgh-ijkl-mnop.
#
#   APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY
#     ─ The CN of your Developer ID Application certificate, exactly
#       as it appears in `security find-identity -p codesigning -v`.
#       Looks like:
#         Developer ID Application: Jake Watts (J4UJD4Z33J)
#       For App Store builds, swap this to the matching Apple
#       Distribution cert when you're ready to submit:
#         Apple Distribution: Jake Watts (J4UJD4Z33J)
#       (We use one env var; flip it depending on which path you're
#       building.)
#
# Lose any of these? Apple lets you regenerate them all from the
# developer portal — but it's quicker to back the cert .p12 up to
# iCloud + Nextcloud the same way you did for the Android keystore.
# See native-fork/src-tauri/macos/SIGNING.md.

APPLE_TEAM_ID=J4UJD4Z33J
APPLE_ID=jakewatts809@googlemail.com
APPLE_PASSWORD=
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY=Developer ID Application: Jake Watts (J4UJD4Z33J)
